          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "goes back to Sanskrit sáṁtāyatē, \"is stretched out, is covered\", and CDIAL lists the Gujarati verb, \"to conceal oneself\" (CDIAL 12887): to be covered over, out of sight. A person hides himself with સંતાવું (santāvũ): સંતાઈ ગયો; a thing is hidden with છુપાવવું."
            }
